<title>USA: Maine firms say workers comp rules may raise costs.</title>
<headline>Maine firms say workers comp rules may raise costs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A hearing on a new bill to alter Maine's workers' compensation rules drew widespread interest, as employers say the legislation would result in a 75-percent increase in workers compensation insurance rates if they were passed into law.</p>
<p>Injured workers testified the reforms that were passed in 1992 have left them without adequate protection.</p>
<p>Gov. Angus King says he would likely veto any major changes in the law.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
